1
00:00:15,196 --> 00:00:17,824
"All I can be is sorry,
and that is all I am."

2
00:00:51,398 --> 00:00:53,567
But I'm afraid you still don't mean it.

3
00:01:25,263 --> 00:01:26,890
We'll try again in the morning.

4
00:01:51,997 --> 00:01:52,998
[BEEPS]

5
00:01:56,293 --> 00:01:57,586
[ELEVATOR BELL DINGS]

6
00:02:06,844 --> 00:02:08,137
See you tomorrow, Helly.

7
00:02:11,808 --> 00:02:13,017
[ELEVATOR BELL DINGS]

8
00:02:13,101 --> 00:02:14,310
[ELEVATOR BELL DINGS]

9
00:02:20,524 --> 00:02:22,233
[BREATHES SHAKILY]

10
00:02:22,317 --> 00:02:23,610
Fuck me.

11
00:02:28,699 --> 00:02:30,742
I read it 300 times yesterday.

12
00:02:32,160 --> 00:02:36,873
259. Again, please. Now.

13
00:02:36,957 --> 00:02:40,251
[MUFFLED SPEAKING]

14
00:02:40,335 --> 00:02:41,836
What the hell is that voice?

15
00:02:46,340 --> 00:02:47,675
[BREATHING SHAKILY]

16
00:02:49,885 --> 00:02:52,430
[BREATHING DEEPLY]

17
00:02:59,687 --> 00:03:03,356
HELLY: "Forgive me for the
harm I have caused this world.

18
00:03:05,275 --> 00:03:07,652
None may atone for my actions but me."

19
00:03:15,326 --> 00:03:17,954
[CRYING] "And only in
me shall their stain live on."

20
00:03:22,584 --> 00:03:26,003
[MUFFLED SPEAKING CONTINUES]

21
00:03:30,466 --> 00:03:32,259
I really am sorry, okay?

22
00:03:32,343 --> 00:03:33,844
[BREATHING SHAKILY]

23
00:03:35,346 --> 00:03:36,513
I'm sorry.

24
00:03:38,766 --> 00:03:41,769
No paraphrasing. Again.

25
00:05:17,151 --> 00:05:18,819
[VIBRATING]

26
00:05:22,614 --> 00:05:24,116
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

27
00:05:28,078 --> 00:05:30,456
[BREATHING SHAKILY]

28
00:06:05,781 --> 00:06:06,948
[SIGHS]

29
00:06:35,726 --> 00:06:36,727
-Mark?
-Yep?

30
00:06:36,811 --> 00:06:41,439
It's past 1100, and Helly's been
in the break room since yesterday.

31
00:06:41,523 --> 00:06:43,899
-Okay?
-I wonder if, as department chief,

32
00:06:43,983 --> 00:06:46,569
you feel you should check on her progress?

33
00:06:46,653 --> 00:06:48,112
-Well…
-Mark doesn't have that power.

34
00:06:48,196 --> 00:06:49,905
-Well, he can ask.
-He's not going to.

35
00:06:49,989 --> 00:06:50,990
-He might.
-Okay…

36
00:06:51,074 --> 00:06:52,492
Hi.

37
00:06:55,412 --> 00:06:57,330
I'm so sorry to interrupt.

38
00:06:58,456 --> 00:07:02,292
We met the other day.
I'm Burt from Optics and Design.

39
00:07:02,376 --> 00:07:06,046
-Hi, Irving.
-Hi, Burt. What are you doing here?

40
00:07:06,130 --> 00:07:07,380
Exactly how the wet fuck do you know

41
00:07:07,464 --> 00:07:08,548
-where this office is?
-Dylan!

42
00:07:08,632 --> 00:07:12,802
My… My predecessor, Alice K., came
here once when they still did the summits,

43
00:07:12,886 --> 00:07:15,180
-and she'd left directions.
-Give us them reversed.

44
00:07:15,264 --> 00:07:16,389
MARK: Okay. It's all right.

45
00:07:16,473 --> 00:07:17,933
What can we do for you, Burt?

46
00:07:18,017 --> 00:07:19,226
Thank you. Well…

47
00:07:20,019 --> 00:07:22,019
Irving, I kept thinking
about what you said

48
00:07:22,103 --> 00:07:25,606
about being excited for
the new handbook totes,

49
00:07:25,690 --> 00:07:27,650
and maybe you were kidding and teasing.

50
00:07:27,734 --> 00:07:29,526
No, not at all.

51
00:07:29,610 --> 00:07:32,863
Okay, good. I've been fretting,
though, because you mentioned

52
00:07:32,947 --> 00:07:36,200
the anticipation could
distract from your work,

53
00:07:36,284 --> 00:07:37,868
which was the opposite of my intent.

54
00:07:37,952 --> 00:07:41,121
So I figured, heck, let's
bring them over now.

55
00:07:41,205 --> 00:07:43,665
That way, it won't be on your mind.

56
00:07:43,749 --> 00:07:48,753
You brought pre-release
handbook totes for us?

57
00:07:48,837 --> 00:07:51,798
It seemed like the right thing.
I know your time is valuable.

58
00:07:51,882 --> 00:07:55,052
Okay, well, you can drop 'em on the desk.
Long hike back to O&D.

59
00:07:55,761 --> 00:07:56,844
Right.

60
00:07:56,928 --> 00:07:59,722
I also wanted to extend an invitation.

61
00:07:59,806 --> 00:08:02,476
Again, I know you… you work hard, so…

62
00:08:03,143 --> 00:08:07,062
If an informal tour of O&D
ever sounds refreshing,

63
00:08:07,146 --> 00:08:11,150
I'd be happy to personally offer
that to Irving and any one of you.

64
00:08:11,942 --> 00:08:14,653
Directions are in the front bag, reversed.

65
00:08:14,737 --> 00:08:15,821
Hard pass.

66
00:08:18,115 --> 00:08:19,784
BURT: [EXHALES SHARPLY] Okay.

67
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:22,870
IRVING: Thank you, Burt.

68
00:08:23,996 --> 00:08:24,996
Thank you.

69
00:08:32,671 --> 00:08:35,756
Just seems soon to be
taking him up on his offer.

70
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:38,802
It's absurd we've never
visited them before now.

71
00:08:39,302 --> 00:08:43,723
Kier's whole original vision
saw us all working together.

72
00:08:43,807 --> 00:08:46,975
That was before O&D started
disemboweling people's bowels.

73
00:08:47,059 --> 00:08:49,395
IRVING: Nonsense. I'll be back by 1:00.

74
00:08:51,105 --> 00:08:53,105
-He's gonna die.
-[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

75
00:08:54,233 --> 00:08:55,234
Irv…

76
00:09:04,326 --> 00:09:05,452
How many times?

77
00:09:08,663 --> 00:09:10,540
1,072.

78
00:09:40,485 --> 00:09:42,335
What about the voice behind the door?

79
00:09:42,696 --> 00:09:43,822
Crying baby, you mean?

80
00:09:45,115 --> 00:09:47,992
No. Like, the angry, mumbly guy.

81
00:09:48,076 --> 00:09:51,829
Guys? We're really not supposed
to talk about the break room.

82
00:09:52,371 --> 00:09:54,081
You know, the important thing is,

83
00:09:54,165 --> 00:09:57,043
you apologized correctly,
and now you're out.

84
00:09:58,085 --> 00:09:59,586
What you gotta do is trick the machine

85
00:09:59,670 --> 00:10:01,713
by thinking about something
you're really sorry about,

86
00:10:01,797 --> 00:10:05,592
so I like to imagine my outie's
love-made with a MILF or two,

87
00:10:05,676 --> 00:10:08,763
which is obviously badass,
but I do pity the husbands.

88
00:10:29,783 --> 00:10:30,867
MARK: Hey.

89
00:10:32,410 --> 00:10:33,910
Break room sucks.

90
00:10:33,994 --> 00:10:38,332
But that's why we have protocols and
procedures so we don't end up there.

91
00:10:39,333 --> 00:10:41,085
You'll learn. I promise.

92
00:10:54,181 --> 00:10:55,182
Hello?

93
00:10:57,058 --> 00:10:58,350
Who's that?

94
00:10:58,434 --> 00:10:59,644
Oh, hi.

95
00:11:00,228 --> 00:11:03,981
It's Irving B. from Macrodata Refinement.

96
00:11:04,065 --> 00:11:06,150
We met in the hall the other day.

97
00:11:09,404 --> 00:11:11,489
Burt's over there by shelf six.

98
00:11:12,448 --> 00:11:13,908
Don't touch anything.

99
00:11:17,035 --> 00:11:20,872
The big envelopes can
handle an appendix reissue.

100
00:11:20,956 --> 00:11:26,461
But, of course, we ship all
the hallway pieces in-frame.

101
00:11:27,879 --> 00:11:30,215
Huh. So much to remember.

102
00:11:31,925 --> 00:11:33,593
Felicia and I make do.

103
00:11:34,177 --> 00:11:38,889
I'm sure it's easier than whatever
you MDR kids get up to all day.

104
00:11:39,807 --> 00:11:43,435
I can only imagine what it's
like when the new art comes in.

105
00:11:43,519 --> 00:11:45,730
I mean, you see it before anyone.

106
00:11:46,689 --> 00:11:51,235
It's so dumb, but I actually cried

107
00:11:51,319 --> 00:11:54,196
when you guys put up <i>The
Youthful Convalescence of Kier</i>.

108
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:55,781
-No.
-I did.

109
00:11:55,865 --> 00:11:59,534
I never thought I'd see the
handbook passage depicted visually.

110
00:11:59,618 --> 00:12:05,999
It was only up for a month or
so, but, man. What a month.

111
00:12:11,671 --> 00:12:12,672
Come here.

112
00:12:14,424 --> 00:12:19,136
Once the hall art's been cycled
through all the departments,

113
00:12:19,220 --> 00:12:21,429
it ends up back here.

114
00:12:21,513 --> 00:12:22,514
Wow!

115
00:12:26,143 --> 00:12:27,644
Where did Felicia go?

116
00:12:27,728 --> 00:12:28,729
Supply run.

117
00:12:32,733 --> 00:12:33,734
Voilà.

118
00:12:39,740 --> 00:12:41,867
"Let not weakness live in your veins.

119
00:12:42,451 --> 00:12:45,036
Cherished workers, drown it inside you."

120
00:12:45,536 --> 00:12:48,581
"Rise up from your
deathbed and sally forth,

121
00:12:49,123 --> 00:12:53,336
more perfect for the struggle."

122
00:12:54,587 --> 00:12:55,588
Exactly.

123
00:12:56,130 --> 00:12:57,131
I…

124
00:12:58,257 --> 00:12:59,509
I can't believe you

125
00:13:01,177 --> 00:13:02,428
you have this.

126
00:13:17,859 --> 00:13:20,362
I'm sorry. What time is it?

127
00:13:20,988 --> 00:13:21,989
I have to go.

128
00:13:39,088 --> 00:13:40,464
Hey, Helly.

129
00:13:41,382 --> 00:13:43,467
-I got to 4%.
-Yes!

130
00:13:43,551 --> 00:13:44,635
Feels good, right?

131
00:13:46,303 --> 00:13:48,888
-I guess.
-Awesome. I'm glad you agree.

132
00:13:52,434 --> 00:13:53,435
Great work.

133
00:15:22,853 --> 00:15:23,854
Hmm.

134
00:15:26,107 --> 00:15:27,108
What's this?

135
00:15:27,900 --> 00:15:29,318
Will you put that away?

136
00:15:31,153 --> 00:15:33,363
-Put what away?
-It's a map of the hallways.

137
00:15:33,447 --> 00:15:34,864
No, it isn't.

138
00:15:34,948 --> 00:15:37,298
Mmm, I thought we weren't
supposed to make maps.

139
00:15:37,742 --> 00:15:39,952
We're not. I didn't.
It's just something I found.

140
00:15:40,036 --> 00:15:41,037
I think Petey made it.

141
00:15:41,121 --> 00:15:42,914
Oh, shit. You didn't turn it in?

142
00:15:43,456 --> 00:15:45,666
-[SIGHS]
-You're such a hypocrite,

143
00:15:45,750 --> 00:15:47,793
lecturing me on following the rules.

144
00:15:47,877 --> 00:15:50,588
I wasn't lecturing you. I'm just trying
to keep you out of the break room.

145
00:15:50,672 --> 00:15:53,122
I can't believe Petey was a mapper.
Let me see it.

146
00:15:53,508 --> 00:15:58,678
He's got wellness, management, perpetuity…
Everywhere we know of.

147
00:15:58,762 --> 00:16:00,347
This must've taken him weeks.

148
00:16:00,431 --> 00:16:02,098
Why aren't we supposed to map the office?

149
00:16:02,182 --> 00:16:05,518
It's an Eagan rule.
"Render not my creation in miniature."

150
00:16:05,602 --> 00:16:06,603
Why?

151
00:16:07,521 --> 00:16:09,022
What the fuck is this?

152
00:16:09,106 --> 00:16:11,441
They look like houses, right?
That's how houses look.

153
00:16:11,525 --> 00:16:15,070
Yeah, exactly, because these
are random, bored doodles.

154
00:16:15,154 --> 00:16:17,905
Well, maybe they're on the outside
and Petey found a way to get to them.

155
00:16:17,989 --> 00:16:20,449
So why would they be on
a map of the severed floor?

156
00:16:20,533 --> 00:16:22,034
It could be a thing. You don't know.

157
00:16:22,118 --> 00:16:23,285
It's not a thing.

158
00:16:23,369 --> 00:16:25,246
Clearly he was trying
to tell you something.

159
00:16:25,330 --> 00:16:26,581
Uh, no.

160
00:16:27,081 --> 00:16:28,791
Go lick a boot, Mark.

161
00:16:30,168 --> 00:16:32,718
You're more loyal to this
place than to your friend.

162
00:16:33,004 --> 00:16:36,840
I'm loyal to how it felt around
here before you showed up.

163
00:16:36,924 --> 00:16:38,175
You mean when Petey was here?

164
00:16:38,259 --> 00:16:40,218
Yeah, because there was balance.

165
00:16:40,302 --> 00:16:44,889
We could have fun and work without
the whole goddamn department imploding.

166
00:16:44,973 --> 00:16:46,432
The work is bullshit.

167
00:16:46,516 --> 00:16:49,769
The work is mysterious and important.

168
00:16:49,853 --> 00:16:52,855
And we deal with the
uncertainty it brings us

169
00:16:52,939 --> 00:16:55,567
in the way that Kier would've wanted.

170
00:16:56,526 --> 00:16:59,154
Together, as a family.

171
00:17:00,655 --> 00:17:04,241
I could not, with a razor to my throat,

172
00:17:04,867 --> 00:17:07,411
be less interested in being your family.

173
00:17:13,376 --> 00:17:16,878
Your best friend left this for
you, and you don't give a shit.

174
00:17:34,396 --> 00:17:36,814
You're right. I don't give a shit.

175
00:17:36,898 --> 00:17:37,899
Mark…

176
00:17:41,611 --> 00:17:45,781
There. It's gone. Thank you, Helly.
Now we can get back to work.

177
00:17:48,993 --> 00:17:50,952
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

178
00:17:51,036 --> 00:17:52,037
Mark!

179
00:17:54,665 --> 00:17:56,125
It's an emergency.

180
00:17:57,042 --> 00:17:59,628
MARK: [SIGHING] Okay. Uh, all right…

181
00:17:59,712 --> 00:18:00,962
I was going to get Mr. Milchick,

182
00:18:01,046 --> 00:18:03,173
but I thought it best not to
break the chain of command.

183
00:18:03,257 --> 00:18:05,633
[CHUCKLES] It's just
raining contraband today.

184
00:18:05,717 --> 00:18:07,567
-What do you mean?
-It doesn't matter.

185
00:18:07,760 --> 00:18:10,471
Has anyone seen anything like this before?

186
00:18:10,555 --> 00:18:12,223
Passage 31, page 110.

187
00:18:12,307 --> 00:18:18,062
"Be content in my words, and dally not
in the scholastic pursuits of lesser men."

188
00:18:18,146 --> 00:18:20,064
No books except the handbook. I know.

189
00:18:22,692 --> 00:18:23,734
IRVING: What are you doing?

190
00:18:23,818 --> 00:18:25,945
His ego's pissed 'cause Helly
called him out for boot-licking.

191
00:18:26,029 --> 00:18:29,323
-My ego's fine. I'm just trying to…
-Damn.

192
00:18:30,115 --> 00:18:31,991
IRVING: Mark, what is this?

193
00:18:32,075 --> 00:18:35,703
Maybe it's another Petey message.
Flip through. See if my name's anywhere.

194
00:18:35,787 --> 00:18:37,581
I bet it's a loyalty test.

195
00:18:38,498 --> 00:18:39,916
Remember the spicy candy?

196
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:41,459
I'll be turning this in to Milchick.

197
00:18:41,543 --> 00:18:44,420
What? Why? It's booty.
It's booty with your name on it.

198
00:18:44,504 --> 00:18:45,630
Excellent decision, Mark.

199
00:18:45,714 --> 00:18:49,114
This is an idolatrous text that
should be brought to him immediately.

200
00:19:15,200 --> 00:19:17,577
So what's their space like?
Stalactites and shit?

201
00:19:17,661 --> 00:19:20,955
No, it's nice. Burt's fostered a
really welcoming environment.

202
00:19:21,039 --> 00:19:23,625
He understands the spirit of Lumon.

203
00:19:25,168 --> 00:19:26,169
Helly?

204
00:19:27,629 --> 00:19:29,547
-[DOOR SLAMS]
-MR. MILCHICK: Excuse me! Helly!

205
00:19:29,631 --> 00:19:30,756
MS. COBEL: Jesus, Helly!

206
00:19:30,840 --> 00:19:32,090
I want a camera!

207
00:19:32,174 --> 00:19:35,510
-I am so sorry, Ms. Cobel. I will…
-What is happening here?

208
00:19:35,594 --> 00:19:38,430
What's happening is, you're
going to give me a video camera

209
00:19:38,514 --> 00:19:43,226
so I can tape a resignation
to my outie right fucking now,

210
00:19:43,310 --> 00:19:46,605
or you're going to have to explain
to her why she's missing four fingers.

211
00:19:46,689 --> 00:19:49,650
Okay. Let's just… [EXHALES SHARPLY]

212
00:19:50,234 --> 00:19:52,069
HELLY: It's Cobel, right?

213
00:19:52,652 --> 00:19:53,653
MS. COBEL: Yes.

214
00:19:54,654 --> 00:19:58,699
Cobel, do I look like I'm
fucking around right now?

215
00:19:58,783 --> 00:20:01,827
No. No, you do not.

216
00:20:01,911 --> 00:20:02,912
MARK: Helly!

217
00:20:04,330 --> 00:20:08,835
MS. COBEL: Hi, Mark.
I'm just catching up with your trainee.

218
00:20:11,921 --> 00:20:13,548
Mr. Milchick,

219
00:20:14,464 --> 00:20:16,883
could you get the video camera, please?

220
00:20:20,929 --> 00:20:22,055
[VIDEO CAMERA BEEPS]

221
00:20:23,473 --> 00:20:24,474
[BEEPS]

222
00:20:42,950 --> 00:20:44,243
Hey.

223
00:21:09,392 --> 00:21:10,393
[BEEPS]

224
00:21:16,941 --> 00:21:21,362
Well, boss. I guess this is the part
where I should tell you to go to hell.

225
00:21:23,197 --> 00:21:24,615
Except you're already here.

226
00:21:33,290 --> 00:21:34,583
I was never sorry.

227
00:21:41,547 --> 00:21:43,007
[ELEVATOR BELL DINGS]

228
00:21:43,091 --> 00:21:44,467
[ELEVATOR BELL DINGS]

229
00:21:53,184 --> 00:21:54,185
[SIGHS]

230
00:21:56,771 --> 00:21:58,064
HELLY: <i>Helly,</i>

231
00:21:59,065 --> 00:22:01,942
<i>I watched your video asking that I resign.</i>

232
00:22:02,526 --> 00:22:06,154
<i>I also received and responded
to your previous request.</i>

233
00:22:06,697 --> 00:22:08,239
<i>I assumed that would resolve the issue,</i>

234
00:22:08,323 --> 00:22:13,537
<i>but now Ms. Cobel says you
threatened to cut off your fingers?</i>

235
00:22:18,041 --> 00:22:22,795
<i>I understand that you're unhappy
with the life that you've been given.</i>

236
00:22:24,130 --> 00:22:27,133
<i>But you know what?
Eventually, we all have to accept reality.</i>

237
00:22:28,175 --> 00:22:31,178
<i>So, here it is.</i>

238
00:22:33,639 --> 00:22:35,391
<i>I am a person.</i>

239
00:22:37,101 --> 00:22:38,477
<i>You are not.</i>

240
00:22:40,187 --> 00:22:41,981
<i>I make the decisions.</i>

241
00:22:43,399 --> 00:22:44,691
<i>You do not.</i>

242
00:22:45,775 --> 00:22:49,612
<i>And if you ever do anything to my fingers,</i>

243
00:22:50,196 --> 00:22:53,658
<i>know that I will keep you alive
long enough to horribly regret that.</i>

244
00:22:56,369 --> 00:22:58,580
<i>Your resignation request is denied.</i>

245
00:22:59,789 --> 00:23:00,790
<i>Turn it off.</i>

246
00:23:17,806 --> 00:23:21,644
MARK: <i>"Welcome your child
into a world surrounded by nature."</i>

247
00:23:22,353 --> 00:23:25,105
No, thanks. Uh…

248
