428
00:39:31,860 --> 00:39:32,945
MDR would.

429
00:39:35,113 --> 00:39:36,114
You're crazy.

430
00:39:36,698 --> 00:39:38,449
I wish I could nap.

431
00:39:39,200 --> 00:39:41,660
I think I sleep 15 hours a night up there.

432
00:39:41,744 --> 00:39:42,995
It's a character flaw.

433
00:39:43,079 --> 00:39:45,289
It just means you're a
party guy, disco king.

434
00:39:45,373 --> 00:39:47,625
I can't be falling asleep, Burt.

435
00:39:47,709 --> 00:39:50,085
-Who cares?
-The handbook cares.

436
00:39:50,169 --> 00:39:54,006
"No workplace shall be
repurposed for slumber."

437
00:39:54,090 --> 00:39:58,552
I know the handbook, old man.
I'm more of a first edition guy.

438
00:40:00,012 --> 00:40:06,684
The original word of Kier: "And I shall
whisper to ye dutiful through the ages.

439
00:40:06,768 --> 00:40:10,605
"In your noblest thoughts and
epiphanies shall be my voice."

440
00:40:10,689 --> 00:40:13,108
"You are my mouth,"

441
00:40:13,692 --> 00:40:17,194
"and through ye, I will whisper on"

442
00:40:17,278 --> 00:40:19,906
when I am ten centuries demised."

443
00:40:22,783 --> 00:40:24,368
I don't understand.

444
00:40:24,452 --> 00:40:28,915
He doesn't just speak to us through
the handbook or the paintings.

445
00:40:29,707 --> 00:40:31,334
He finds other ways.

446
00:40:34,545 --> 00:40:36,339
MARK: "You think you need your job.

447
00:40:38,007 --> 00:40:40,383
"But I've lived abroad as a vagrant,"

448
00:40:40,467 --> 00:40:45,263
"abstaining from my own money
to rely on the charity of strangers."

449
00:40:45,847 --> 00:40:49,768
"Most were beggars
themselves, yet they were happy."

450
00:40:50,518 --> 00:40:53,438
"And so, for that summer, was I."

451
00:40:55,398 --> 00:40:57,734
"Your job needs you,"

452
00:40:59,110 --> 00:41:01,278
not the other way around."

453
00:41:07,034 --> 00:41:09,370
